A||||3||jlruiz67||Porting manifolds question||||5||
Z||000000||jlruiz67||11-25-2000||09:41 PM||||I read this on a auction on ebay. Does anyone know if this is true???<P>"Porting BOTH manifolds nets you an 8 horsepower increase in the upper RPMs<BR>on EVERY V6 Fiero. This is a dynoed result that many Fiero List members<BR>have done. Porting one side, I'm assuming would give you 4 horsepower, you<BR>will notice a difference with just one. There are no problems with doing<BR>just one becuase it's equalized at the Y-pipe."<BR><p>[This message has been edited by jlruiz67 (edited 11-25-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||hugh||11-26-2000||08:53 AM||||<BR>"Porting BOTH manifolds nets you an 8 horsepower increase in the upper RPMs<BR>on EVERY V6 Fiero. This is a dynoed result that many Fiero List members<BR>have done. Porting one side, I'm assuming would give you 4 horsepower, you<BR>will notice a difference with just one. There are no problems with doing<BR>just one becuase it's equalized at the Y-pipe."<BR>By both manifolds they meant intake and exhaust.The reason for porting is to improve flow whether it is air or exhaust gases.One of the goals in modifying an engine is to balance the output of all the cylinders,you treat them as individual engines and try to make them as even as possible.If you do just the intake you will see some improvement.If you were to do just one exhaust side you could run lean on those cylinders because of the improved flow through them.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||11-26-2000||12:12 PM||||I have seen that add on e-bay.  It is in reference to the exhaust manifolds.  I believe the consensus here is that it does net you some HP at the expense of a little torque.  WEhether it is 8HP or not is for the guys that have access to dynos.<P>I would have to agree with Hugh that if you only do one side you may have an imbalance  in fuel delivery and the engine may not run optimally.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||jlruiz67||11-26-2000||12:58 PM||||Thank you very much for your responce. I got the one rear exhaust manifold for $17.50, in the future I will find the front and then I will port them both and install them.||||reg||1
